IMPORT prelude

-- Skills Development Levy Act 1979 (Singapore) -- who must pay (s 2 "employer", "employee", "wages"), how much (s 3), and the
-- penalties for false returns (s 11) and their composition (s 17).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/SDLA1979.txt (version
-- in force from 1 July 2026; s 3 as amended by Act 4 of 2023, in force 15 June 2023).
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0004 (subjects/sg/requirements.jsonl), raised by the cradle-to-grave-simone scenario
-- (event e041): what levy is payable for one employee whose monthly remuneration is $4,200.
--
-- THE FIGURES ARE IN THE ACT. REQ-0004 expected the rate, floor and cap to be in regulations. As deposited, s 3 states all
-- three: 0.25% of wages, at least $2, and no levy on wages above $4,500 a month -- each "or such [other] rate/amount as the
-- Minister may, by notification in the Gazette, prescribe". No such notification was retrieved; the encoding takes the
-- figures in s 3 as the figures in force, which is an assumption about the Gazette, not a reading of it.
--
-- NOT ENCODED: the exemption orders (s 4), the Skills Development Fund (ss 5-10, 20), enforcement powers (ss 14A, 15), the
-- wages the Minister has excluded by notification (s 2 "wages"), and the regulations on returns and payment dates.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table, no
-- independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Skills Development Levy Act 1979 -- the levy`

§§ `2 -- who is an employee`

-- s 2: "employee" means one "rendering in that month services wholly or partly in Singapore" (or on leave earned by such
-- services), "but does not include any domestic servant, gardener or chauffeur, wholly and exclusively employed by an
-- individual otherwise than in connection with his or her trade, business, profession or vocation". "employer" means "any
-- person who pays or is liable to pay any wages to an employee".
DECLARE Worker IS ONE OF
    `an office employee in Singapore`
    `a part-time shop assistant in Singapore`
    `a domestic helper employed privately by a household`
    `a private chauffeur employed by an individual for personal use`
    `a chauffeur employed by an individual for the individual's business`
    `an employee working wholly outside Singapore`

GIVEN `the worker` IS A Worker
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the worker is an employee for the levy` IF
    CONSIDER `the worker`
    WHEN `a domestic helper employed privately by a household` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a private chauffeur employed by an individual for personal use` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `an employee working wholly outside Singapore` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `3 -- the amount`

-- s 3(1): every employer must, for each employee, "pay a skills development levy of the greater of the following amounts:
-- (a) subject to subsection (2), an amount calculated at the rate of 0.25% of the wages in any month of that employee ...;
-- (b) $2." (2): "the levy is not chargeable on the part of the wages of the employee in any month that exceeds $4,500".
-- So the levy is never less than $2 and never more than 0.25% of $4,500 = $11.25 a month.
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the levy rate` MEANS 0.0025

GIVETH A NUMBER
`the wage ceiling` MEANS 4500

GIVETH A NUMBER
`the minimum levy` MEANS 2

GIVEN `monthly wages` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the chargeable wages` MEANS
    IF `monthly wages` GREATER THAN `the wage ceiling` THEN `the wage ceiling` ELSE `monthly wages`

GIVEN `monthly wages` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the monthly levy for one employee` MEANS
    IF `the chargeable wages` `monthly wages` TIMES `the levy rate` GREATER THAN `the minimum levy`
    THEN `the chargeable wages` `monthly wages` TIMES `the levy rate`
    ELSE `the minimum levy`

GIVEN `the worker` IS A Worker, `monthly wages` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the levy payable for the worker` MEANS
    IF `the worker is an employee for the levy` `the worker`
    THEN `the monthly levy for one employee` `monthly wages`
    ELSE 0

§§ `11, 17 -- false returns`

-- s 11(1): negligently or without reasonable excuse making a false return or giving false information -- "a penalty equal to
-- the amount of the levy due and unpaid and ... a fine not exceeding $2,500 or ... imprisonment ... not exceeding 6 months
-- or ... both". (2): wilfully with intent to evade -- "a penalty equal to double the amount of the levy due and unpaid and ...
-- a fine not exceeding $5,000 or ... imprisonment ... not exceeding 3 years or ... both".
-- s 17(1): the Agency may abate a penalty or compound an offence for "a sum not exceeding $1,000". (The deposit's arrangement
-- numbers this section 15A; the body numbers it 17.)
DECLARE Falsity IS ONE OF
    `negligent or without reasonable excuse`
    `wilful with intent to evade`

GIVEN `the falsity` IS A Falsity, `levy due and unpaid` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the penalty for a false return` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the falsity`
    WHEN `wilful with intent to evade` THEN `levy due and unpaid` TIMES 2
    OTHERWISE `levy due and unpaid`

GIVEN `the falsity` IS A Falsity
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine for a false return` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the falsity`
    WHEN `wilful with intent to evade` THEN 5000
    OTHERWISE 2500

GIVEN `the falsity` IS A Falsity
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum imprisonment in months for a false return` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the falsity`
    WHEN `wilful with intent to evade` THEN 36
    OTHERWISE 6

GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum composition sum` MEANS 1000
